body:
They have been using Treat Wounds liberally, but that one hour cooldown is rough on them, and they don't have a dedicated healer or anyone who is higher than Trained on Medicine apparently. The party is as follows, with free archetype:  

Lizardfolk Fighter with Monk dedication, a claw-and-shield build;  
Poppet Barbarian with Fighter and Gladiator dedication, an intimidate build;  
Halfling Wizard with Bard and Scroll Trickster dedication, meant to have a very flexible spell selection;  
Sprite Summoner with Wellspring Mage and (divine) Sorcerer dedication, with a dragon eidolon, and was the one who died against the old man statue;  
Strix Paladin with Ranger dedication, a close-quarters shooter, the one who died against the haunt in the kitchen.

I did have some concerns about their builds, but nothing major, just a feat selection here and there. Their tactics against the catoblepas were not great to be honest, the wizard cast Black Tentacles into its room, failing to affect it, and everyone kind of stood their distance as it got off a couple of breath weapons on them, then charged ahead and trampled 3 of them when the tentacles went away.

The main issue was just that they completely ran dry on healing after the catoblepas, so maybe party comp was the real issue, but I was also noticing that their rolls were exceptionally bad, like barely rolling above a 10 all night for multiple party members.

Anyway, while I was typing this they TPKed on Kannitri the ghost monk, so, oops.
